Themes deliberately not included, and why.

**None of the registration numbers below were read at tsdr.uspto.gov.** That
source stayed closed on every attempt: the page is JavaScript gated and the API
now answers HTTP 401, asking for a key. What is recorded here is second-hand —
searches, and where noted a cross-check against public mirrors of the USPTO
record. Read these as the reason a name was set aside, not as findings of fact.

One of them was corroborated. **ATOM, US Reg. 4,819,136** — the reason this
package's constructor is `oneDark` and not `atomOneDark` — matches on two
independent mirrors: serial 86315816, owner GitHub, Inc., registered
2015-09-22, International Class 009, goods "Downloadable computer software for
use in developing and editing computer software." That description covers code
editors directly. Still a mirror, not the register itself.

    Dracula         Search reports US Reg. 6,306,339 (Zeno Rocha) naming
                    "syntax highlighters" among its goods. MIT conveys no
                    trademark rights.
    Nord            Search reported US Reg. 7,458,940 (NordSec B.V.). That
                    number could not be corroborated on any mirror. What does
                    appear is a NORD mark held by NordSec (serial 88768969) in
                    security-software goods, and several sibling marks
                    (NORDVPN, NORDPASS, NORDSEC). Nord's licence was clean —
                    MIT, (c) 2016-present Sven Greb, read directly — and the
                    name is the only reason it is absent. Failing to find a
                    registration is not evidence there is none, so the
                    conservative side of the open question is the one taken:
                    Nord stays out.
    GitHub Dark/Light   GITHUB is a live mark and GitHub's brand policy
                    restricts name use separately from the MIT licence.
    Everforest      Search reports US Reg. 7,762,715 and EUIPO 018641989.
    Monokai Pro     Proprietary; may not be sub-licensed or redistributed.
                    This one is a licence term, read directly, not a search.

The licence findings above are a record of reading each project's LICENSE file.
The trademark lines are a record of database searches, one of them cross-checked
